# Privacy Policy — Lock n' Pop

**Last updated:** August 2026

Lock n' Pop ("the app") is a companion reference app for the game Deadlock. This policy explains what information the app does and does not collect.

## What we collect

**We do not collect, store, or transmit any personal information.**

The app has no user accounts, no sign-in, and no server of our own. Specifically:

- **Favourites** (heroes and items you star) are saved only on your own device, using standard local app storage. This information never leaves your phone and is never sent to us or anyone else.
- **We do not use analytics, tracking, or advertising SDKs of any kind.**
- **We do not collect your name, email, location, or any device identifiers.**

## Data from third parties

The app displays live game data (hero stats, item prices, images) by making standard network requests to a public, community-run game data service. These are anonymous requests for public game information — no personal or identifying data about you is sent as part of these requests.

## Children's privacy

The app is not directed at children and does not knowingly collect information from anyone, regardless of age, since it does not collect personal information from any user.

## Changes to this policy

If this policy changes in the future (for example, if new features are added that do handle personal data), this page will be updated and the "Last updated" date above will reflect that.

## Contact

Questions about this policy can be sent to: locknpop2026@outlook.com

## Disclaimer

Lock n' Pop is an unofficial fan-made companion app. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Valve Corporation. Deadlock and all related assets are the property of Valve Corporation.
